.TH CFILE 1 "2026" "CFile 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cfile \- interactive command line file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfile
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfile
starts an interactive session for listing, searching, copying, moving,
renaming and removing files and directories. Destructive operations always
ask for confirmation, and existing files are never overwritten silently.
.PP
Paths accept a leading \fB~\fR and may be quoted with single or double
quotes. A backslash escapes the next character.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colors. Colors are also disabled when standard output is not a
terminal, when \fBTERM\fR is \fBdumb\fR, or when \fBNO_COLOR\fR is set to a
non-empty value.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-banner
Do not print the banner and command menu at startup.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ls [\-a] [dir]
List a directory with permissions, sizes and modification times. Directories
are listed first. \fB\-a\fR includes hidden entries.
.TP
.B cd [dir|\-]
Change directory. Without arguments goes to \fB$HOME\fR; \fB\-\fR returns to
the previous directory.
.TP
.B pwd
Print the current directory.
.TP
.B find <name> [dir]
Recursive, case-insensitive search by file name (substring match). Symbolic
links are not followed. At most 200 results are shown.
.TP
.B info <path>...
Show type, size, permissions (symbolic and octal), owner, link count, inode
and timestamps. For directories the recursive size is included.
.TP
.B cp <src> <dst>
Copy a regular file. If \fIdst\fR is a directory the file is copied into it.
Asks before overwriting.
.TP
.B mv <src> <dst>
Move a file or directory. Asks before overwriting. Moving a directory to a
different filesystem is not supported.
.TP
.B rename <path> <name>
Rename an entry within its directory. Never overwrites.
.TP
.B rm <file>...
Remove files after confirmation. Directories are refused.
.TP
.B mkdir [\-p] <dir>...
Create directories; \fB\-p\fR also creates missing parents.
.TP
.B rmdir <dir>...
Remove empty directories after confirmation.
.TP
.B clear, help [command], quit
Clear the screen, show the menu or help for one command, leave the program.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a normal exit, 1 if the starting directory cannot be entered, 2 for
invalid command line options.
.SH FILES
CFile does not read or write any configuration files.
